# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WebClient environment variables (Vite). Copy to `.env.local` for local
# overrides, or set per-environment `.env.<mode>` files. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code; VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET is read
# by vite.config.ts at dev-server start (not shipped to the browser).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL the browser uses for /api and /hubs requests.
#   - Leave EMPTY for same-origin deployments (the SPA is served by the same
#     host that exposes the API — WPF-embedded host on :5200 OR standalone
#     WebApi). One build works against either host with no rebuild.
#   - Set to an absolute URL (e.g. http://controller-host:5200) only for
#     split-origin deployments where the SPA and API are on different origins.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Dev-server proxy target for `npm run dev`. The Vite dev server forwards
# /api and /hubs (WebSocket) to this host. Point it at whichever backend you
# are developing against:
#   - http://127.0.0.1:5200  → WPF-embedded controller host (default)
#   - http://127.0.0.1:<port> → standalone WebApi host
VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:5200
